3. tinfoilsh/tinfoil-go
-----------------------

Source:    https://github.com/tinfoilsh/tinfoil-go
Revision:  branch `feat/v3`
License:   Apache-2.0
Copyright: Tinfoil, Inc.

Two substantial files in this crate -- roughly 70 KB together, about a third of
the source -- are **not** from tinfoil-rs and were previously unrecorded here.
They are new Rust ports of the corresponding Go packages in tinfoil-go, which
is where the v3 verification model is defined:

    src/provenance.rs  (32 KB)  <- verifier/provenance  (`AuthenticateCode`,
                                   platform endorsements, freshness witnesses)
    src/policy.rs      (36 KB)  <- verifier/policy      (machines map, TDX/SEV
                                   appraisal, VM shape, measurement resolution)

These are ports rather than vendored copies: the structure follows the Go
packages and the security decisions are deliberately the same, but no Go source
was translated line by line, and the error handling, type layout and tests are
this crate's own.

`src/attestation/envelope.rs` and `src/attestation/tdx.rs` in the sibling
`cvm-vault` crate likewise port `verifier/envelope` and `verifier/quote/tdx`
from the same branch. They are noted here because the wire formats they
implement are defined by that project.


4. Test fixture: assets/rekor_test_bundle.json
----------------------------------------------

A genuine, publicly logged Sigstore bundle, retained verbatim as a test
fixture. It is third-party data rather than code, and is reproduced here
because verification can only be meaningfully tested against real evidence:
every signature in it -- the DSSE signature, the embedded SCTs, the Rekor
inclusion proof, checkpoint and signed entry timestamp, and the Fulcio chain --
is real and is checked by the tests.

    Artifact:       tinfoilsh/confidential-model-router @ v0.0.75
    Bundle format:  application/vnd.dev.sigstore.bundle.v0.3+json
    Rekor logIndex: 1186330805
    sha256:         de603b00072997dabfd7f7be899fe622ab63db6c200cca60f475ad4babe2212e

The corresponding artifact and log entry are public records of the Sigstore
transparency log. Copyright in the signed statement rests with Tinfoil, Inc.
